/0    0   1   _ _  _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _ _   NORTH _
; PROCESS and REDO must reach tables above 127: table n, not n-128.
; HI -> PROCESS 129 prints HIGH129 (LOW1 = table 1 = wrapped target).
; RE -> PROCESS 130, whose REDO must restart table 130, not table 2:
;       REDO PASS1 then REDO PASS2 (LOW2 = table 2 = wrapped target).
; Table 3 is the input loop and never falls off (jDAAD ends the game
; when process 0 runs out), so every path in it ends in REDO.
/PRO 0
> _ _   CLS
        MESSAGE 0
        PROCESS 3
/PRO 1
> _ _   MESSAGE 1
/PRO 2
> _ _   MESSAGE 2
/PRO 3
> _ _   PARSE 0
        REDO
> _ _   PROCESS 4
        REDO
/PRO 4
> HI _  PROCESS 129
        DONE
> RE _  PROCESS 130
        DONE
